{"title":"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A shopper plans to purchase an item that has a listed price greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751f8354c64df7687207c0df786c41cc883ab3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and can use any one of the three coupons. Coupon A gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a8787ca8fcdf64f42e938d20fa64f63871646d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> off the listed price, Coupon B gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a22960968e6c093c4eae61303577e4f90fd4051c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> off the listed price, and Coupon C gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/96633b73a86b9d9110e1ff824fce08def96ca296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> off the amount by which the listed price exceeds\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/751f8354c64df7687207c0df786c41cc883ab3cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textdollar 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. <br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the smallest and largest prices, respectively, for which Coupon A saves at least as many dollars as Coupon B or C. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d2d36ed8ae2ac20e4bcec402980a11639c40c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441abba6b58bf5f746fc848106bba86a7dbf1fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 50 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 60 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 75 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 80  \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the listed price be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9409f7f27a664469d23090938f11f296adb48d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100 + p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bf07ceb43df8c7388742c5c1a3667791306791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Coupon A saves us: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8ff7c32806fecbd109777eb7f7841c5f5ca2c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.15(100+p) = (0.15p + 15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Coupon B saves us: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Coupon C saves us: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d4350c0f34738387e88729bb2d1d2f57043f0b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.25p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Now, the condition is that A has to be greater than or equal to either B or C which gives us the following inequalities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c313515101fd135bcc4c84f65708b151c738ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\geq B \\Rightarrow 0.15p + 15 \\geq 30 \\Rightarrow p \\geq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"293\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/2586348ff8cc0eaf479802af67fe8278a418e7f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\geq C \\Rightarrow 0.15p + 15 \\geq 0.25p \\Rightarrow p \\leq 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"316\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We see here that the greatest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60a455408724093e429b12e66bf2afb874f050c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 100 + 150 = 250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" /> and the smallest value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/2013c432d62fd99b89da7804b8124ddb2918c61c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 100 + 100 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6cb0f062afdb3a20d26b182b2a640e0779156d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - x = 250 - 200 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"232\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vYXz4wStBUU\">https://youtu.be/vYXz4wStBUU</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B\">2010 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a hre